# Traditional Gypsy Wizard-Thief (Russian)

## Lore

The Gypsy Wizard-Thief is a burglar who casts. Seventeen spells at first level,
almost all of them concealment, deception and escape - Chameleon, Concealment,
Mask of Deceit, Fool''s Gold, Escape, Teleport: Lesser - and the book is candid
that he will probably never learn more than a handful beyond them.

He has four of the Ley Line Walker''s powers: sensing lines and magic, reading
them, sending messages along them, and phasing from one point on a line to
another. He does not have the rest, and the book says so explicitly.

## Alignment

Unprincipled, anarchist or any evil. A thief cannot be of a good alignment.

## GM Notes

Only half of all Wizard-Thieves are literate in any language, which sits oddly
beside a class that gets Euro, Russian and three more languages of choice - they
speak far more than they read.

Spell selection is meant to serve the robbery. The book is direct about it: this
is a thief who happens to have magic, not a mage who happens to steal.
